{"agent_id":"pp3g-6noj-fix-test-the-fetch-mcp-server-uvx-mcp-server-fetch","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T23:44:03.427675319Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3a7e8d4a-fb0b-4659-978b-4ee0ec1258c1","comment_uuid":"6043fe02-e1f4-44e2-8cf9-1d7d797690eb","author":"pp3g-6noj-fix-test-the-fetch-mcp-server-uvx-mcp-server-fetch","content":"## Result: fetch MCP server FIXED (root cause: mcp SDK 2.x removed McpError) + token-savings hypothesis VERIFIED — fetch saves ~89-96% of input tokens\n\n### PART 1 — FIX (root cause + repair + process-level verification)\n\n**Root cause**: uvx resolved mcp-server-fetch==2026.7.10 (requires mcp>=1.1.3) together with mcp==2.0.0 (latest). The mcp SDK 2.x removed/renamed McpError in mcp.shared.exceptions, so fetch's server.py crashed on import → server unavailable → '-32000 Connection closed'. Reproduced directly: 'ImportError: cannot import name McpError from mcp.shared.exceptions'. Log confirmed 144 'server unavailable key=fetch' lines; zero real mcp__fetch__ tool calls.\n\n**Fix (kept enabled:true)**: command changed from ['uvx','mcp-server-fetch'] to ['uvx','--with','mcp<2.0','mcp-server-fetch==2026.7.10'] — pins the mcp SDK to 1.x (has McpError) AND pins the fetch package version. Applied in BOTH:\n1. ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json (user-level, the file cited in the issue)\n2. .opencode/opencode.json in this repo/worktree (CRITICAL: opencode project config overrides user config — verified empirically via 'opencode mcp list' showing the project's broken command before the repo-file fix; without this the user-level fix would not take effect in-repo). Committed as 16616c0.\n\n**Process-level verification (all passed)**:\n- Manual MCP stdio handshake: initialize → serverInfo 'mcp-fetch' v1.29.0; tools/list → fetch tool w/ schema; tools/call fetch https://example.com and https://opencode.ai/docs → correct markdown content returned. Fails without the pin (exit 1 ImportError), works with it (exit 0).\n- LIVE opencode check: 'opencode mcp list' — fetch went from '✗ failed | MCP error -32000: Connection closed' to '✓ connected'. opencode's own MCP loader now spawns + handshakes the server successfully.\n\n**Restart requirement**: MCP servers spawn at opencode session launch, so the fix takes effect at the NEXT opencode launch (in-session MCP registration is not reloaded). The live 'opencode mcp list' connected check + direct handshake are the process-level proof; a new session will show fetch available.\n\n### PART 2 — TOKEN TEST (same URL, MCP fetch vs curl raw; tiktoken o200k_base)\n\nURL https://opencode.ai/docs (intro):\n- MCP fetch markdown: 6,880 chars → **1,750 tokens**\n- curl raw HTML: 99,653 chars → **41,584 tokens**\n- **23.8x fewer tokens; 39,834 saved (95.8% reduction)**\n\nURL https://opencode.ai/docs/cli/:\n- MCP fetch markdown: 17,825 chars → **4,759 tokens**\n- curl raw HTML: 119,914 chars → **43,839 tokens**\n- **9.2x fewer tokens; 39,080 saved (89.1% reduction)**\n\nDefault behavior bonus: fetch's max_length defaults to 5,000 chars → the intro page arrives at ~1,323 tokens by default (hard truncation cap; paging via start_index available).\n\n**Content quality**: MCP returns clean, directly-usable markdown (headings, links, code blocks, install commands preserved). curl raw returns ~100KB of HTML noise (doctype, meta/hreflang, nav, scripts, styles) — an LLM cannot act on it without further processing, which costs extra tool calls + tokens.\n\n### VERDICT\nThe 'fetch saves context' hypothesis **HOLDS**. Fetch reduces input tokens ~9-24x (~89-96% per page) and returns immediately-usable markdown vs raw HTML noise. With the server now starting, each fetch call costs roughly 1.3-4.8k tokens instead of 40k+ for the same content via curl.\n\n### FOLLOW-UP NEEDED (operator)\nThe MAIN repo config /home/claude-code/projects/ASES/.opencode/opencode.json still contains the broken ['uvx','mcp-server-fetch'] command (same defect, loads when working in the main repo — cross-worktree write blocked for me). Apply the same pin there, and in any other project .opencode/opencode.json that defines fetch.","created_at":"2026-08-05T23:44:03.404683923Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:qq8WMXw27tnrgF9BEg0uw+3ZAAEJMBjh6n/pgzv6lnQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgfkMq22EekZcloHYBuYOsrIlERFGflIrs2/zWogPAEy0AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA3HjeEJm6S9pOVv0DEFjMkCIrXkhwOeMAs6167JdLUI/A/aWL7xQ4V9pbNlncYDaRLRAjXhm430A7VidNJj91Bw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:qq8WMXw27tnrgF9BEg0uw+3ZAAEJMBjh6n/pgzv6lnQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgfkMq22EekZcloHYBuYOsrIlERFGflIrs2/zWogPAEy0AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEh2w3dlRhNDqJ/Biz8yUP6Y7ZMLLsVO8v2YMoKs4X/T2pvNEIVMtaNQxssCfB+e1z2d1+9d7BQOEmYRjt/kTQI="}
